# Changelog

All notable changes to the WiFiMCU firmware project will be documented in this file.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-11-10 (Modern Community Edition)

### Added
- **`cjson` Module:** Native, high-performance embedded JSON parser and serializer with `cjson.encode()` and `cjson.decode()` in `lua/exlibs/cjson.c`.
- **`sntp` Module:** Network Time Protocol client with UDP socket sync, hardware RTC timestamp setting, and timezone offset support (`sntp.sync()`, `sntp.time()`, `sntp.setoffset()`).
- **Standardized Firmware Output:** Renamed build output artifact to `WiFiMCU_Firmware_v1.0.0.bin`.
- **Python Flashing Tool:** Automated YModem flashing script under `tools/flash_firmware.py`.

### Fixed
- **MQTT Hard Fault on `lmqtt_new`:** Fixed ARM Cortex-M4 uninitialized memory crash by enforcing clean zero-allocation and disabling default SSL pointers in `lua/exlibs/mqtt.c`.
- **MQTT Socket Memory Leak:** Reclaimed ~1KB per reconnect socket buffer via `MQTTClientDeinit`.
- **Graceful FreeRTOS Thread Teardown:** Fixed hanging threads and reclaimed task stack when MQTT socket disconnects.
- **GPIO `INPUT_PULL_UP` Bug:** Fixed invalid macro mapping in `lua/exlibs/gpio.c`.
- **Compiler Encoding Errors:** Removed corrupted non-ASCII characters in `net.c` preventing modern IAR builds.

---

